    "preamble": "Sadanand Sharma vs The State Of Bihar on 3 February, 2020 Author: Anil Kumar Upadhyay Bench: Anil Kumar Upadhyay In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.5944 of 2020 Arising Out of Ps. Case No.-1 Year-2019 Thana- Government Official C District- Banka ====================================================== Sadanand Sharma Son of Late Kartik Sharma Resident of Village - Vishwakarma Nagar, Katoria, P.S.- Katoria, Distt.- Banka. ... ... Pe Versus The State of Bihar ... ... Opposite Party/s ====================================================== Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Ajay Mukherjee, Advocate For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Parmeshwar Mehta, A.P.P. = == == == = ===================== = Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Anil Kumar Upadhyay Oral Order",
    "facts": "The petitioner is in custody in connection with F.S. Case No. 01 of 2019 for the offenses under Sections 26(2) (1) of the Food Safety & Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the allegation against the petitioner in the instant case is that he has used substandard mirch powder in his restaurant. Learned counsel for the petitioner further submits that the FSL report does not indicate that the mirch powder was found dangerous to life.",
